new='''#ifndef GUT_XCHG
#define GUT_XCHG 0
#endif
// KVLDS (KERNELS.md G4b, research/3.9): §2.9's lever on the key side. A
// workgroup is WAVES waves of QT query tiles each, and a key block's K and V
// tiles are fetched once by the workgroup -- KV_STAGE uvec4 a lane a plane,
// a block ahead, in flight behind the previous block's MMAs -- and written
// to two LDS planes the waves read their fragments from: K as BN key rows of
// the head's components at K_LPITCH halves, V^T as HEAD_DIM component rows
// of the block's keys at V_LPITCH (both 2 dwords mod 32, conflict-free for
// the sixteen lanes of a ds_load_b64). One plane each, so two barriers a
// block: after the S^T reads (K's plane is rewritten behind it) and after
// the O^T reads (V's). The same MMAs in the same order per accumulator as
// the one-wave build at the same KTIL: bit-identical. A wave whose queries
// start past the sequence runs the loop (the barriers need it) and stores
// nothing. KV_NOBAR and KV_STAGE_L0 are pricing knobs, wrong by
// construction: no barriers; every staging fetch the first block's.
#ifndef KVLDS
#define KVLDS 0
#endif
#ifndef WAVES
#define WAVES 1
#endif
#ifndef KV_NOBAR
#define KV_NOBAR 0
#endif
#ifndef KV_STAGE_L0
#define KV_STAGE_L0 0
